WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.930
MTF Agents scramble through the crowd of bloodthirsty,
hypnotized festival-goers.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.880
Up on the stage, a pair of living statues
hold down a screaming man as they produce

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.550
medieval instruments of torture from an antique
case.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.100
Maybe this time, the agents can stop it.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.640
Maybe they can prevent all the horror and
bloodshed.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.310
But one thing stands in their way: A man-sized,
cartoonish dove costume, flying down towards

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:33.000
them, wielding a large wooden mallet that
would only bring death and destruction.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.450
Needless to say, even by Foundation standards,
this one is going to be weird…

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.360
When you found yourself sought out by the
SCP Foundation’s recruitment division and

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.910
offered a role in the research department,
they made sure to inform you of the risks.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.739
After all, a workplace injury in this line
of work might be far more serious than slipping

00:00:52.739 --> 00:00:57.129
on a wet floor, or developing carpal tunnel
from typing all day.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:01.550
Working within the ranks of the Foundation,
you could be the unfortunate victim of any

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:07.380
number of dangerous anomalies, whether its
SCP-096 appearing behind you after you accidentally

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.060
caught a glimpse of it as a single pixel in
a photo.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.560
Or if you were in the wrong place at the wrong
time whenever SCP-682 next broke out, then

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.490
chances are you’d be receiving an early
redundancy… and a closed casket service,

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.270
if there’s even enough of you left to bury.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.880
It is the one thing you never want to happen.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.320
The scenario you’re constantly warned about
from the moment you join the Foundation: a

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.290
containment breach.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.340
Anything can be the cause of an anomaly breaking
free of containment and spreading untold chaos

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.720
in the process.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.070
Whether it’s the result of a particularly
cantankerous SCP that doesn’t take kindly

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:50.720
to being locked up, an act of earnest human
error with disastrous consequences, or even

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:57.479
intentional sabotage enacted by a group of
interest trying to seize anomalies for their

00:01:57.479 --> 00:01:58.479
own purposes.

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:03.479
There’s no telling when or where a containment
breach might occur… or is there?

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:08.080
Despite all the resources at their disposal
– specialized facilities spanning the globe,

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.910
advanced technology, and a nearly inexhaustible
supply of personnel to contain SCPs – the

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:19.610
Foundation still manages to suffer catastrophic
casualties as a result of containment breaches.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.950
But surely, if they’re so well equipped,
such breaches should be almost impossible,

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:25.950
right?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:26.950
Well, yes.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.930
So, what causes them?

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.879
What if every containment breach, all the
loss of life, the further spread of anomalies,

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:39.230
and the destruction of Foundation of property
incurred, was all caused… by an SCP?

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.709
Not a living entity, mind you.

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:46.280
More some kind of latent anomalous phenomenon
that triggers containment breaches without

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.280
warning.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:52.420
The prevailing theory surrounding this phenomenon
is even itself considered to be an SCP within

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.659
its own right, referred to as SCP-001.

00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:01.489
Of course, as many of those well-versed in
the history and practises of the SCP Foundation

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:07.530
will already know, SCP-001 is a designation
shared by a number of anomalies.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.930
Some are believed to actually exist, while
others are speculated to just be falsified

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:16.500
covers created to mask the real SCP-001.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.260
From beings such as the Gate Guardian and
the Scarlet King, to the existence of God’s

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:27.240
Blind Spot and even the Foundation itself,
each of these SCP-001’s are nicknamed after

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.530
the Foundation researcher who proposed them
for the designation, and often considered

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:37.450
to be some of the first, if not the very first,
anomalies ever encountered – or at least,

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.450
documented.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.459
In that regard, this SCP-001 – Plague’s
Proposal – could well be one of the very

00:03:43.459 --> 00:03:49.220
first latent anomalies to exist, explaining
why so many SCPs were uncontained prior to

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:54.319
the Foundation being established, and why
even now, with all their resources, containment

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:58.090
breaches are still a worryingly frequent occurrence.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.829
There are multiple anomalies that appear to
have been directly affected by SCP-001, at

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:07.220
least, according to the research of one of
the Foundation’s Directors, Director Lague.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:11.560
While he might be drawing conclusions and
seeing patterns where there aren’t any to

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.530
speak of, Lague reasons that the circumstances
of these specific recorded containment breaches

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.130
seem to indicate that SCP-001 was at fault.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:26.290
The first of these incidents Director Lague
focuses on in his research is also the one

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.000
we’ll be focusing on for the remainder of
this video.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.900
It is designated as SCP-001-1.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:41.039
SCP-001-1 previously went under the designation
of SCP-5770, and is an annual, anomalous event

00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:45.330
that occurs in the Piazza della Signoria in
Florence, Italy.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.620
The event consists of an unscheduled festival
that goes on for a period of ten days, wherein

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:56.250
anyone present within a ten-kilometer range
of the affected area suffers a mind-altering

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.160
effect that compels them to attend the festival.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:05.650
However, SCP-001-1 is not a well-documented,
long-running festival of great cultural significance

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:10.030
to the people of Florence, neither is it an
event that is widely advertised.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:14.729
Yet, those who have experienced the psychic
draw of this anomalous festival are driven

00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:16.280
to attendance.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:21.520
During the course of SCP-001-1, two anomalous
entities that resembled the statues created

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.280
by Michelangelo during the Renaissance will
host a show wherein they take to a stage to

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.030
judge people that they deem to be sinners.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:33.289
This pair of statue creatures will call upon
the audience and bring those they’ve designated

00:05:33.289 --> 00:05:39.050
sinners up onto the stage with them and will
then enact makeshift, grueling punishments.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.190
These have been noted to resemble the acts
depicted in Dante Alighieri’s Inferno, so

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.729
if you ever need any further proof of how
hellish these punishments are, we recommend

00:05:47.729 --> 00:05:49.650
asking an art expert.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:55.830
The moment that SCP-001-1 ceases and the festival
comes to a close, any and all in attendance

00:05:55.830 --> 00:06:01.000
are subject to yet another form of anomalous
mental alteration, and will proceed to instantly

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.600
forget the event.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:07.470
Any of the horrific torture performed on stage
becomes unknown to those that directly witnessed

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:11.230
it, leaving them unaware of anything that
occurred only moments prior.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:16.160
So, given the Foundation’s extensive knowledge
of this festival, its gruesome proceedings

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:21.210
and the effects it has on those in attendance,
you might be forgiven for expecting them to

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.750
have a fairly well-established method of keeping
the event contained.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:29.960
Presumably, setting up a cordon to keep attendants
out of the area, administering amnestics to

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.849
any that might have been affected by SCP-001-1’s
anomalous mind-altering.

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:41.110
But then you remember SCP-001, the theory
behind what could be the cause of containment

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.110
breaches.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:45.680
As a result, the Foundation has still been
unable to establish containment of the event

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:52.830
formerly known as SCP-5770, and Director Lague’s
research has tied this issue with containment

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:59.960
to SCP-001, hence the festival’s redesignation
to SCP-001-1.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:03.780
Following the initial discovery of an anomalous
annual occurrence in the city of Florence

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:11.690
in 1985, the SCP Foundation’s head researcher
assigned to what was then known as SCP-5770

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:16.390
was one Joseph Pasqua, former Site Director
at Site 322.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:21.000
Pasqua was, according to the incidents recorded
on the Foundation’s own database, somehow

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.030
manipulated by one of the anomalous statue
creatures that performed the show during occurrences

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:27.310
of SCP-5770.

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:32.949
It was thanks to the influence of this entity
that Joseph Pasqua deserted his post at the

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:35.880
Foundation, and went into hiding.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.340
The fact that the influence of one of the
‘performers’ of this festival was able

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:44.289
to extend its influence to a senior member
of Foundation staff was not only troubling,

00:07:44.289 --> 00:07:46.960
but also constituted a containment breach.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.560
Pasqua would later be tracked down by Foundation
agents operating in and around Italy.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:57.020
He was discovered thirty years after his desertion
in Vatican City, as a member of the Papal

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.979
Conclave – a specially selected group of
Catholic cardinals that are charged with electing

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:03.259
a new Pope.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:07.480
If the former Site Director was still being
influenced by the statue creatures, it is

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:11.520
highly likely that he had spent the previous
three decades climbing the ranks of the Catholic

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.569
Church, potentially to install a new Pope
at the behest of the entities responsible

00:08:16.569 --> 00:08:20.199
for conducting the torture of the Florence
festival.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:23.860
Another recorded incident of a containment
breach surrounding the event, that seemed

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:29.810
to lend credence to the existence of SCP-001,
the anomalous cause of breaches, occurred

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:33.430
the year following SCP-5770’s discovery.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:38.090
In 1986, the Foundation was observing the
proceedings of the festival as part of their

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:41.380
ongoing investigation into its bizarre nature.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:46.860
On site were agents of Mobile Task Force Zeta
66, better known under their unit’s codename

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.510
of the ‘Guardian Angels.’

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:54.390
During the festival, MTF Zeta 66 operatives
noticed the presence of a previously unknown

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.180
entity associated with the anomalous event.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:02.399
The Foundation was already aware of the pair
of seemingly living Michelangelo sculptures,

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:09.220
designating them as SCP-5770-1 and SCP-5770-2
respectively.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:16.019
This third entity, despite being given the
designation SCP-5770-3, had its own preferred

00:09:16.019 --> 00:09:18.120
identification for itself.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:23.220
The being referred to itself as ‘God’s
Strongest Soldier’ and resembled a mascot

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:25.060
costume of a dove.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:29.590
Approximately two meters tall, this creature’s
body was entirely hollow – there was nothing

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:33.630
within the costume, the costume was its body.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:39.000
The responding agent of MTF Zeta 66, codenamed
Zeta Turquoise, was the first to confront

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.490
God’s Strongest Soldier, and was greeted
with quite the opener.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.950
“Tweedley-dee, tweedley-da.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.560
God’s strongest soldier is my name.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.220
Getting rid of sin is my game.”

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:52.220
Confused at the creature’s demeanor and
presence, Zeta Turquoise called in a report

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:57.250
to command, stating that a large bird man
was harassing random attendants of the festival.

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:03.140
When Turquoise moved in to confront SCP-5770-3,
the creature repeated its assertion that it

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:07.730
was God’s Strongest Soldier, and that its
aim was to get people into heaven.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:11.350
The Agent requested that God’s Strongest
Soldier get out of his way, he had a job to

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:14.980
do, but the bizarre bird-man responded with
more whimsical nonsense.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:19.670
“Burgers, sandwich, fruit, and fries, you
just told me a big, fat lie!”

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:21.230
God’s Strongest Soldier proclaimed.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.579
“Tweedley deedopa, didapa di dowop, papa-doda!”

00:10:25.579 --> 00:10:31.720
Upon Zeta Turquoise attempting to push past
the creature, SCP-5770-3 produced an oversized

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.260
wooden mallet seemingly from out of thin air.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:38.930
It then wound its arms back and immediately,
viciously struck the MTF agent.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:43.660
A low-orbit Foundation satellite reported
not long after that an object had been detected

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.000
existing the Earth’s stratosphere.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.450
Analysis confirmed it was, indeed, Zeta Turquoise.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:55.240
Yes, he was literally punted into earth’s
orbit by a cartoonishly large wooden mallet.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:59.320
As for the entity known as God’s Strongest
Soldier, the bird-like creature then proceeded

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:04.250
to attack the other members of Mobile Task
Force Zeta 66 in a similar fashion, making

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:08.180
sure they got to heaven in every sense of
the phrase.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:12.500
With multiple recorded instances of containment
breaches occurring in relation to the festival

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.970
in Florence, and happening so frequently,
more and more evidence of Director Lague’s

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:20.170
theory about SCP-001 was being validated.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:25.660
In 1988 the Foundation attempted a different,
more pacifistic approach to containing the

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.720
annual ‘celebration’, by attempting to
cordon off the entrance to the area of Florence

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.390
where those compelled to attend the festival
usually congregated.

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:38.269
There was additionally a cover story issued
to the public, stating that this was done

00:11:38.269 --> 00:11:43.170
as a quarantine measure to keep residents
away from an area hosting a potentially dangerous

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:44.300
infection.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.389
For a time, this seemed to be working.

00:11:46.389 --> 00:11:50.459
The streets were quiet, local residents seemed
to be going about their business and paying

00:11:50.459 --> 00:11:53.160
little mind to the Foundation operative in
the area.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:58.060
That is, until the mind-altering effects of
SCP-001-1 took hold.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:03.130
A mass of people, estimated to be over one
hundred thousand Florentines, charged towards

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:04.779
the cordoned-off area.

00:12:04.779 --> 00:12:09.420
This mass of people swept through like a tidal
wave breaking through a dam, causing Foundation

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.940
personnel to be trampled alive.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.850
Those that survived the initial rush were
attacked by civilians, in what seemed to be

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.680
a coordinated effort to reach the gathering
area for the festival.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:24.680
All Foundation agents in the area were terminated
in short order, mercilessly slaughtered and

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:29.810
then cannibalized before anything that remained
of their bodies was dumped into the Arno River

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.810
nearby.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:35.459
As well as being evidence of the sheer mental
alteration the statue creatures and the festival

00:12:35.459 --> 00:12:39.990
itself were capable of, for Director Lague,
this seemed to indicate something further.

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:46.770
If an anomaly, SCP-001, was truly responsible
for all containment breaches, allowing them

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:51.790
to occur in spite of the measures taken to
prevent such things happening, then the phenomena

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:56.190
seemed to be occurring specifically to prevent
the Foundation from achieving containment

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.740
of certain SCPs.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:13:03.660
Lague’s theory developed with every passing
breach that involved SCP-001-1.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:08.150
In theory, the festival should have been an
average Tuesday for Foundation staff, a relative

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:12.510
walk in the park in order to contain it, if
not to outright stop it from happening at

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:13.510
all.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:18.149
Yet, despite all their resources, manpower,
and expertise in all things anomalous, the

00:13:18.149 --> 00:13:20.790
Foundation had been thwarted at every turn.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:24.970
Despite how illogical such occurrences seemed,
containment breaches were still occurring

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:31.240
at an alarming rate, and perhaps none more
so than in relation to SCP-001-1.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:36.750
The following year, 1989, brought with it
the most inexplicable breach yet, and further

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:39.430
proof for Director Lague’s theory about
SCP-001.

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:44.880
While the previous breaches were undoubtedly
anomalous in nature, each always carried with

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:50.589
it the possibility that somehow, despite the
low odds, the Foundation missed something.

00:13:50.589 --> 00:13:54.510
Some human error or previously undiscovered
information about the festival could have

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:59.560
led to Pasqua’s alteration, or the arrival
of God’s Strongest Soldier.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:04.839
But this time, it was undeniable that a force
beyond the scope of the Foundation’s understanding

00:14:04.839 --> 00:14:09.699
was altering reality to prevent them from
containing the festival in Florence.

00:14:09.699 --> 00:14:15.339
An invisible barrier manifested at every entry
point to the main area of the anomalous event,

00:14:15.339 --> 00:14:18.790
whenever a member of Foundation personnel
tried to get in on foot.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.949
Those that attempted to access the festival
area via rappelling out of helicopters instantly

00:14:22.949 --> 00:14:27.550
caught ablaze and burned to death the moment
they touched down on the ground.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:32.960
Any helicopter transports also crashed on
their return journey to Site 322, and God’s

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:37.100
Strongest Soldier was seen trampling on the
wreckage, before flapping its arms and flying

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.100
away.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:41.660
It was following this incident that Lague
was promoted to the potion of Site Director

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:47.610
for Site 322, as a replacement for Joseph
Pasqua, who was still missing at this time.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:52.070
The newly-appointed Director was yet to devise
his theory that there existed an anomalous

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.540
cause for all containment breaches.

00:14:54.540 --> 00:15:00.730
However, during his introductory briefing,
he was presented with the file regarding SCP-5770,

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:07.820
and the various examples of it not being uncontainable,
but being very good at not being contained.

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:11.970
Director Lague asked if some of the more standard
methods had been attempted; at this point,

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.820
the Foundation had tried aerial bombardments
of the festival, Scranton Reality Anchors

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:21.070
to counteract whatever anomalous force was
preventing containment, even using SCP-682

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:22.230
to clear the area.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.959
It had all failed.

00:15:23.959 --> 00:15:27.389
Figuring out why was now Director Lague’s
job.

00:15:27.389 --> 00:15:32.009
All the information of previous failed attempts
to contain the festival led Lague to the conclusion

00:15:32.009 --> 00:15:35.339
that SCP-001 must exist.

00:15:35.339 --> 00:15:41.019
An unseen phenomenon, the missing piece of
the puzzle, the element specifically interfering

00:15:41.019 --> 00:15:42.769
with the Foundation’s efforts.

00:15:42.769 --> 00:15:47.769
He presented his proposal to the Overseer
Council, who were skeptical, to say the least.

00:15:47.769 --> 00:15:52.690
They posited that the statues and bird mascot
creature might be smarter than the latter’s

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:55.160
outwardly cartoonish nature portrayed.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:16:01.440
But this is exactly what, to Director Lague,
indicated SCP-001 was responsible.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:07.199
He explained that all in attendance at the
SCP-5770 festival took the event seriously.

00:16:07.199 --> 00:16:11.710
But the appearance of God’s Strongest Soldier
was an abnormality, whose demeanor and tone

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:16.089
were drastically different from the rest of
the rather cutthroat proceedings.

00:16:16.089 --> 00:16:20.199
Director Lague explained that the sheer absurdity
of this creature seemed to be the result of

00:16:20.199 --> 00:16:24.380
SCP-001 interfering with their operations.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:28.779
After all, if some other cause was to blame
– like an unknown cult attacking Foundation

00:16:28.779 --> 00:16:32.600
personnel when they attempted to contain the
festival – then there would be evidence

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:36.740
of that, and Lague would have no reason to
suspect that God’s Strongest Soldier was

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.819
anything more than just a tonally dissonant
part of the festival.

00:16:40.819 --> 00:16:45.700
Of course, Director Lague couldn’t prove
the existence of SCP-001 based on the presence

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.680
of one cartoonish bird mascot at a festival.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:53.649
But before long, more and more breaches would
start occurring that seemed to further prove

00:16:53.649 --> 00:16:55.470
that Lague was on to something.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:17:00.259
There was something else at work, causing
containment breaches that put the entirety

00:17:00.259 --> 00:17:02.510
of the Foundation in jeopardy…

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:08.709
Now check out “SCP-001 WHEN DAY BREAKS”
and “SCP-001 WHICH IS THE REAL 001?”

00:17:08.709 --> 00:17:09.209
for more!

